oof, a Lean ref or an entry in the block's own Lean inventory. The first is elementary and true (lcm(3,4,5) = 60, verified); the second is explicitly conditional ('Assume both routes produce a Bloch class with archimedean image 2/(3pi)'), so it is a conditional statement wearing an unconditional label. Per AGENTS.md 3b a provable-kind assertion inside a conjecture cone needs either the conditional-class treatment or demotion. Separately, 'By the Birman-Hilden theorem, 3-braid closures yield hyperbolic knots up to 10 crossings' misattributes: Birman-Hilden theory concerns branched coverings and mapping class groups and says nothing of the kind, and the claim as stated is false in any case, since 3-braid closures realise knots of arbitrarily many crossings.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":3},{"id":"trap-negation-contrast","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"STANDING-TRAP FINDING, report only: the Markov-closure table under 'Hyperbolic knots from normal-form closures' is wrong in three of its five rows. Computed the component count of each H_3 basis element's closure from the induced permutation on 3 strands: identity -> 3 components (table says '3 disjoint unknots', CORRECT); sigma_1 and sigma_2 -> 2 components each, i.e. a 2-component unlink, but the table says 'unknot'; sigma_1 sigma_2 and sigma_2 sigma_1 -> 1 component each, i.e. an unknot, but the table says 'Hopf link L_H'; sigma_1 sigma_2 sigma_1 -> 2 components, the Hopf link. The table's L_pm and Hopf-link rows are therefore swapped with the sixth basis element, and the last row compounds it: it labels the sixth element 'e^- = sigma_1^3, trefoil 3_1 = T(2,3)', but sigma_1^3 is a 2-braid and is not an element of the H_3 normal-form basis at all - the sixth basis element is sigma_1 sigma_2 sigma_1, whose closure is the Hopf link, as the sibling def:breit-wheeler-pair-production also gets wrong. Corrected table: 1 -> 3-unlink; sigma_1, sigma_2 -> 2-unlink; sigma_1 sigma_2, sigma_2 sigma_1 -> unknot; sigma_1 sigma_2 sigma_1 -> Hopf link. The section's conclusion ('No basis element closes to a hyperbolic knot') survives unchanged - none of the six is hyperbolic either way.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":3},{"id":"trap-nonspeakable","group":"Voice","result":"fail","severity":"minor","notes":"proposed: 'Q(zeta_5) has no imaginary quadratic subfield; its only proper subfield is the real quadratic Q(sqrt 5).' and 'approximately 30 prime knots'. Minor: trailing whitespace on five lines.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":3},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"Voice","result":"fail","severity":"major","notes":"proposed: convert each to an explicit sub-conjecture or hypothesis ('Assume every hyperbolic knot ... appears in this set'), since the reduction argument depends on them. Structural: this is six sentences across four sections.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":3},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"Voice","result":"fail","severity":"minor","notes":"proposed: keep the first, delete the other two, or make the later ones explicit back-references. Not fixed inline: they sit in three different sections and removing them changes each section's closing shape.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":3},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"STANDING-TRAP FINDINGS, report only, never fix math inline. (1) LAMBDA-vs-Cl_2, the AGENTS.md guard, live in content/: Observation 2 writes 'Vol(B_3) = 8G = 8 Cl_2(pi/4)'. The VALUE 8G = 7.327724753 is right; the NAME is not. Recomputed: Cl_2(pi/4) = 0.9818721511, so 8 Cl_2(pi/4) = 7.854977208, which is not Vol(B_3). G = Cl_2(pi/2) = 0.9159655942. The Lobachevsky form is Vol(octahedron) = 8 Lambda(pi/4) = 4G = 3.663862377, and Vol(B_3) = 2 octahedra = 8G. This block's own sibling tbl:bloch-wigner-mathlib-filler-table1-data has it right (4 Cl_2(pi/2) = 4G), so the corpus disagrees with itself one file over. Proposed fix: 'Vol(B_3) = 8G = 8 Cl_2(pi/2)'. (2) FIELD INCONSISTENCY: the boxed conjecture and both reduction claims (C-Hyp), (C-Hodge) live in B(Q(zeta_15)) with F = Q(zeta_3, zeta_5), but the Borromean class has trace field Q(i) = Q(zeta_4), and i is NOT in Q(zeta_15) (Q(zeta_n) contains i iff 4 | n; 4 does not divide 15). So the field the conjecture is stated over cannot contain one of the two classes the argument is built on - and Observation 2 has already concluded the compositum must be Q(zeta_60). The Lean lemma two_knot_decomposition_insufficient, which combines D[Z_{4_1}] and D[Z_{B_3}], is likewise not statable in B(Q(zeta_15)). Proposed fix: state the conjecture over Q(zeta_60), r_2 = 8, and drop the '4-dimensional space' claim in the Reduction section. (3) DUPLICATE LINK: the Observation-3 atlas lists the Borromean rings as the proton/neutron knot AND L6a4 as the 3-He knot, with the same volume 7.328 and the same trace field Q(i) - because L6a4 IS the Borromean rings (6^3_2 in Rolfsen). The Reformulation then treats this as a derived fact ('The shared volume identity 8G establishes the relation B_3 ~ L6a4'), when it is an identity of the same link with itself, and the 'rank-4 atlas-spanned lattice' therefore has at most rank 4 for a different reason than the one given. (4) FORCE-SECTOR MISLABEL: Observation 4 calls T(2,9) and T(3,5) 'the strong-force pair'. This block's own Framing paragraph identifies them as the force carriers producing q[9]_q[10]_q, which is 1/alpha_EM - electromagnetic, per prop:em-coupling-projection. (5) The field table itself is CORRECT throughout: degrees 2, 2, 4, 4, 16 and r_2 = 1, 1, 2, 2, 8 all recomputed via phi(n)/2; r_2(Q(zeta_15)) = 4; the two Lean rank identities 4 = 1 + 2 + 1 and 8 = 4 + 1 + 3 check out arithmetically, though the '+1' and '+3' are bookkeeping constants rather than structure. Vol(6_2) = 4.401 and Vol(8_11) = 8.286 are correct, as is (2/(3pi))/Cl_2(pi/3) = 0.2090826, not a small rational.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":true,"history":3},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","model":null,"at":"2026-08-09","stale":true,"history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"Agentic heuristic check: pass.","reviewer":"agent","by":"one-voice-audit","model":null,"at":"2026-07-19","stale":true,"history":2},{"id":"voice-author-notes-pollution","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","model":null,"at":"2026-08-09","stale":true,"history":1},{"id":"voice-branch-jargon","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"[EXPIRED-NO-FIELD-HASH] No branch/audit working labels, agent status markers or first-person work narration found in the .md body or the .ts title.","reviewer":"agent","by":"local/one-voice-audit","model":null,"at":"2026-08-08","stale":true,"history":1},{"id":"voice-editorializing","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","model":null,"at":"2026-08-09","stale":true,"history":1},{"id":"voice-emoji-content","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","model":null,